1
00:00:01,375 --> 00:00:04,584
<i>Run, until we reach</i>

2
00:00:04,792 --> 00:00:08,709
<i>Until we reach you</i>

3
00:00:14,083 --> 00:00:17,042
<i>The clear blue open sea</i>

4
00:00:17,667 --> 00:00:20,083
<i>A sliver of a miracle</i>

5
00:00:21,125 --> 00:00:26,792
<i>We've encountered more
Than we could ever imagine</i>

6
00:00:27,209 --> 00:00:29,917
<i>With every step
We take on this journey</i>

7
00:00:29,918 --> 00:00:33,334
<i>The goal is still out of sight</i>

8
00:00:33,542 --> 00:00:37,209
<i>But we can overcome anything</i>

9
00:00:37,417 --> 00:00:40,417
<i>Just to see your smile</i>

10
00:00:40,584 --> 00:00:44,542
<i>If we wavered,
We couldn't shine</i>

11
00:00:44,876 --> 00:00:48,375
<i>We even strove to conquer
Our weaknesses</i>

12
00:00:48,626 --> 00:00:53,667
<i>We, who were truly devoted</i>

13
00:00:54,083 --> 00:00:57,999
<i>Have always been the same</i>

14
00:00:58,000 --> 00:00:59,876
<i>Run</i>

15
00:01:00,125 --> 00:01:06,125
<i>Until we reach
Until we reach you, hey</i>

16
00:01:06,751 --> 00:01:10,042
<i>Less than legendary?</i>

17
00:01:10,209 --> 00:01:13,167
<i>No problem! It's all good!</i>

18
00:01:13,334 --> 00:01:15,792
<i>Until the day we can laugh</i>

19
00:01:15,959 --> 00:01:20,667
<i>Follow the shining map</i>

20
00:01:20,876 --> 00:01:26,083
<i>So, no more hesitation, fighter
It's gonna be alright</i>

21
00:01:33,751 --> 00:01:35,667
Unforgivable.

22
00:01:36,375 --> 00:01:37,959
My room...

23
00:01:39,209 --> 00:01:41,709
I mean, my temple...

24
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:45,000
[tense music]

25
00:01:45,584 --> 00:01:46,792
My pets...

26
00:01:47,292 --> 00:01:49,000
[clears throat]

27
00:01:49,292 --> 00:01:51,167
I mean, my servants.

28
00:01:55,751 --> 00:01:58,041
You are but living toys.

29
00:01:58,042 --> 00:02:00,751
I will not suffer this insult.

30
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:05,334
Return my Livedolls!

31
00:02:07,918 --> 00:02:11,834
Destroy the Miniature Garden
Escape Block Kingdom!

32
00:02:14,209 --> 00:02:17,834
How dare you ruin
my perfect kingdom!

33
00:02:19,125 --> 00:02:21,584
You will suffer.

34
00:02:22,751 --> 00:02:24,792
Who is that
on Lord Iscat's back?

35
00:02:24,918 --> 00:02:26,416
Tell us, great Sun God,

36
00:02:26,417 --> 00:02:28,124
how may we quell your fury?

37
00:02:28,125 --> 00:02:29,709
[screaming]

38
00:02:30,792 --> 00:02:32,876
[growling]

39
00:02:36,167 --> 00:02:37,209
Look!

40
00:02:37,501 --> 00:02:39,708
There's a flame up in the sky!

41
00:02:39,709 --> 00:02:40,958
A sign of the end.

42
00:02:40,959 --> 00:02:42,209
This must be stopped.

43
00:02:42,542 --> 00:02:44,791
Or the world will perish.

44
00:02:44,792 --> 00:02:47,042
Do you think you can escape me?

45
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:49,375
Face your Destroyer!

46
00:02:49,501 --> 00:02:52,125
Yikes, this guy's terrifying.
Who is he?

47
00:02:52,250 --> 00:02:53,791
And how is he a god?

48
00:02:53,792 --> 00:02:55,833
Looks more like a damn demon.

49
00:02:55,834 --> 00:02:57,792
I wish I could put him
in his place.

50
00:03:02,501 --> 00:03:04,083
[shaking] Which way?

51
00:03:04,209 --> 00:03:05,501
Um... right!

52
00:03:08,375 --> 00:03:10,292
Come out, Iscat.

53
00:03:11,250 --> 00:03:12,709
There you are!

54
00:03:12,918 --> 00:03:14,459
[meowing]

55
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,167
Hold, miscreants!

56
00:03:20,834 --> 00:03:22,834
Hey, Luffy, look! The town!

57
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:23,917
Wow!

58
00:03:23,918 --> 00:03:26,125
Do you think we can
get over that steep hill?

59
00:03:26,250 --> 00:03:29,167
The sun guy made
this whole place out of blocks?

60
00:03:29,292 --> 00:03:31,000
That's cool!

61
00:03:31,125 --> 00:03:33,626
You're not here
to admire the guy's toys.

62
00:03:36,876 --> 00:03:37,709
He's coming!

63
00:03:37,834 --> 00:03:38,918
We can't slow down!

64
00:03:39,042 --> 00:03:40,625
So, should we go around or what?

65
00:03:40,626 --> 00:03:41,666
I'll cut through.

66
00:03:41,667 --> 00:03:43,082
Nah, I'll kick it down.

67
00:03:43,083 --> 00:03:44,000
Wee!

68
00:03:44,918 --> 00:03:47,083
Oh! Oh! We're going to crash!

69
00:03:47,209 --> 00:03:49,542
Do something!

70
00:03:50,292 --> 00:03:53,459
Hey, cat! Let's fly!

71
00:03:55,292 --> 00:03:57,334
Lord Iscat.

72
00:03:59,876 --> 00:04:02,042
[LUFFY laughs]

73
00:04:02,209 --> 00:04:05,209
[ALL frightened]

74
00:04:08,667 --> 00:04:11,083
It took lots of work
to make this place.

75
00:04:11,209 --> 00:04:13,375
I don't want to wreck it
unless I have to.

76
00:04:18,834 --> 00:04:20,166
[ALL screaming]

77
00:04:20,167 --> 00:04:21,459
Watch for that!

78
00:04:29,292 --> 00:04:31,000
Hey, look out!

79
00:04:32,626 --> 00:04:33,541
I got you.

80
00:04:33,542 --> 00:04:34,501
You're safe.

81
00:04:34,667 --> 00:04:36,375
Nice timing. Thank you.

82
00:04:36,751 --> 00:04:38,292
All right, you're fine. Off.

83
00:04:39,459 --> 00:04:40,292
You, too.

84
00:04:40,459 --> 00:04:41,292
Huh?

85
00:04:41,626 --> 00:04:42,666
Well, damn.

86
00:04:42,667 --> 00:04:44,459
That cat sure
made a mess of things.

87
00:04:44,584 --> 00:04:46,792
[exhales] Should've let me
cut through.

88
00:04:47,417 --> 00:04:49,750
I know you weren't trying
to break things, Cat.

89
00:04:49,751 --> 00:04:51,292
But be careful next time.

90
00:04:51,542 --> 00:04:52,834
[meowing]

91
00:04:56,375 --> 00:04:59,125
Such unbridled recklessness.

92
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:03,542
You would destroy
the world I have created!

93
00:05:04,876 --> 00:05:07,000
Unforgivable!

94
00:05:08,083 --> 00:05:09,125
Get ready!

95
00:05:10,959 --> 00:05:12,751
- [LUFFY] Okay, Cat!
- [meowing]

96
00:05:15,501 --> 00:05:17,626
It's time to go!

97
00:05:25,250 --> 00:05:27,000
Foolish Iscat.

98
00:05:27,709 --> 00:05:31,292
Why are you lending your aid
to these lawless aliens?

99
00:05:31,584 --> 00:05:33,542
Halt, I say!

100
00:05:38,501 --> 00:05:41,500
At this rate, we'll make it
to the other side in no time.

101
00:05:41,501 --> 00:05:44,083
Yeah? Seems like
it goes on forever to me.

102
00:05:44,250 --> 00:05:46,124
Come on, Luffy, just look.

103
00:05:46,125 --> 00:05:48,625
The blueprint has
all the information we need to--

104
00:05:48,626 --> 00:05:49,541
No!

105
00:05:49,542 --> 00:05:50,918
Are you nuts, Nami?

106
00:05:51,083 --> 00:05:52,666
I memorized it all.

107
00:05:52,667 --> 00:05:53,458
We're good.

108
00:05:53,459 --> 00:05:55,042
[screaming]

109
00:05:55,209 --> 00:05:56,209
Wait, really?

110
00:06:00,083 --> 00:06:01,125
See that there?

111
00:06:01,375 --> 00:06:03,291
It's the reflection
of that mirror door

112
00:06:03,292 --> 00:06:04,208
we broke through.

113
00:06:04,209 --> 00:06:05,584
Oh, you're right.

114
00:06:05,792 --> 00:06:07,500
And the clouds aren't even real.

115
00:06:07,501 --> 00:06:09,166
They're just big balls
of cotton.

116
00:06:09,167 --> 00:06:10,042
Huh?

117
00:06:15,334 --> 00:06:16,959
Wow, they really are.

118
00:06:18,292 --> 00:06:20,291
This place looked huge,
but in the end,

119
00:06:20,292 --> 00:06:22,374
it really is just
some big guy's room.

120
00:06:22,375 --> 00:06:24,167
There are mirrors
on all four sides,

121
00:06:24,292 --> 00:06:26,709
so it looks like
the land goes on forever.

122
00:06:26,959 --> 00:06:28,584
We can reach a wall easy.

123
00:06:28,751 --> 00:06:30,292
We just need to go straight.

124
00:06:30,751 --> 00:06:33,542
In fact, we're already halfway
through this place.

125
00:06:33,709 --> 00:06:35,417
We'll be done in a flash.

126
00:06:37,125 --> 00:06:38,750
Ah, I see.

127
00:06:38,751 --> 00:06:39,333
Hmm?

128
00:06:39,334 --> 00:06:42,583
Verily, thou hast witnessed
the blueprints,

129
00:06:42,584 --> 00:06:44,918
but they do not reveal all.

130
00:06:45,250 --> 00:06:46,417
Wait, Val?

131
00:06:46,542 --> 00:06:48,542
Why is he talking
like a samurai?

132
00:06:48,667 --> 00:06:51,166
This was a holding cell
for giants

133
00:06:51,167 --> 00:06:53,124
before I repurposed it.

134
00:06:53,125 --> 00:06:54,042
A net?

135
00:06:55,834 --> 00:06:57,082
If we get captured,

136
00:06:57,083 --> 00:06:59,082
there's no telling
what he'll do to us.

137
00:06:59,083 --> 00:07:01,250
Any way to make
this cat go faster?

138
00:07:04,834 --> 00:07:07,459
It was designed
to be inescapable!

139
00:07:07,584 --> 00:07:08,959
If it's all giants,

140
00:07:09,083 --> 00:07:11,334
what hope do you have?

141
00:07:20,959 --> 00:07:22,501
Curse you, heathens!

142
00:07:22,626 --> 00:07:24,375
[ALL] That was your own fault!

143
00:07:26,792 --> 00:07:30,125
Even if you reach the wall,
it matters not!

144
00:07:30,709 --> 00:07:34,459
You'll never be able
to break it!

145
00:07:34,834 --> 00:07:37,834
[ALL screaming]

146
00:07:40,042 --> 00:07:44,501
In fact, even if you escape,
you'll just reach a dead end.

147
00:07:44,792 --> 00:07:45,999
He got us!

148
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,124
He's so close!

149
00:07:47,125 --> 00:07:48,708
What are we supposed to do now?

150
00:07:48,709 --> 00:07:51,082
Cat, how come you didn't dodge?

151
00:07:51,083 --> 00:07:52,625
[meowing]

152
00:07:52,626 --> 00:07:55,209
[laughs mischievously]

153
00:07:55,417 --> 00:07:57,083
What happened to Lord Iscat?

154
00:07:57,209 --> 00:07:59,167
Who are those people
riding on his back?

155
00:07:59,667 --> 00:08:03,000
Now come with me,
you accursed Livedolls.

156
00:08:03,125 --> 00:08:06,334
I'll put you right back
where you belong.

157
00:08:06,709 --> 00:08:09,584
[meowing loudly]

158
00:08:10,125 --> 00:08:12,918
[laughs mischievously]

159
00:08:14,709 --> 00:08:16,083
You know what to do.

160
00:08:18,918 --> 00:08:20,042
Keep moving!

161
00:08:20,209 --> 00:08:22,250
[dramatic music]

162
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,250
We're free!

163
00:08:38,417 --> 00:08:41,209
Iscat, back.

164
00:08:41,459 --> 00:08:43,416
These wires are made of metal

165
00:08:43,417 --> 00:08:44,959
and they toss straight through!

166
00:08:47,501 --> 00:08:50,083
[growling]

167
00:08:50,292 --> 00:08:52,291
Struggle all you like,

168
00:08:52,292 --> 00:08:54,000
but I am the author of this tale

169
00:08:54,125 --> 00:08:56,209
and the script is unchanged!

170
00:08:56,375 --> 00:08:58,583
You know the rules, Iscat!

171
00:08:58,584 --> 00:09:00,834
The price of treason is death!

172
00:09:02,083 --> 00:09:04,083
[meowing]

173
00:09:05,250 --> 00:09:07,459
He said he's had enough
of your oppression!

174
00:09:07,584 --> 00:09:08,500
What?

175
00:09:08,501 --> 00:09:11,250
How dare you speak
to your master like that!

176
00:09:11,375 --> 00:09:13,541
Your bravado is meaningless

177
00:09:13,542 --> 00:09:16,792
because the vicious Ear God
lies ahead!

178
00:09:16,959 --> 00:09:19,125
Please stop this, Master Iscat!

179
00:09:20,417 --> 00:09:22,334
Sun God, wait!

180
00:09:22,834 --> 00:09:25,125
There's a bit of bad news
about the Ear God.

181
00:09:25,250 --> 00:09:28,626
He died in a fire today
under mysterious circumstances.

182
00:09:28,751 --> 00:09:31,667
We knew it was an ill omen
the moment that it happened!

183
00:09:32,083 --> 00:09:34,501
Then the sky itself
began to crack!

184
00:09:34,959 --> 00:09:37,083
Bigstein Castle's been
damaged too!

185
00:09:37,209 --> 00:09:39,000
Now Lord Iscat has gone mad!

186
00:09:39,125 --> 00:09:41,584
This is truly a cursed day!

187
00:09:42,918 --> 00:09:44,626
They failed Glutbunny.

188
00:09:44,918 --> 00:09:49,334
My vicious, carnivorous rabbit
was reduced to bones!

189
00:09:52,626 --> 00:09:55,374
By the time we realized
what was happening,

190
00:09:55,375 --> 00:09:57,375
this was all that remained.

191
00:10:00,125 --> 00:10:02,876
[screaming]

192
00:10:04,417 --> 00:10:06,959
Sun God,
please contain your fury.

193
00:10:09,834 --> 00:10:11,918
We-we beg of you.

194
00:10:13,417 --> 00:10:16,417
[laughing]

195
00:10:18,042 --> 00:10:19,292
Is this good or bad?

196
00:10:20,876 --> 00:10:22,667
Magnificent!

197
00:10:22,918 --> 00:10:24,500
This is life!

198
00:10:24,501 --> 00:10:26,375
This is world building!

199
00:10:27,709 --> 00:10:32,375
Unscripted drama right here
in my own garden.

200
00:10:33,209 --> 00:10:34,459
What a thrill!

201
00:10:34,584 --> 00:10:36,417
I underestimated them.

202
00:10:37,334 --> 00:10:39,250
I have created a world

203
00:10:39,375 --> 00:10:42,125
where heroes
and villains are born,

204
00:10:42,292 --> 00:10:44,834
along with the deepest lore!

205
00:10:45,209 --> 00:10:47,709
And these Livedolls
and their character arcs

206
00:10:47,834 --> 00:10:49,375
have perfected it!

207
00:10:49,501 --> 00:10:52,375
[laughing]

208
00:10:54,250 --> 00:10:56,417
What the heck
is that guy laughing at?

209
00:10:56,834 --> 00:10:59,584
[laughing]

210
00:11:14,876 --> 00:11:17,876
[laughing]

211
00:11:23,626 --> 00:11:24,750
Hey, come on.

212
00:11:24,751 --> 00:11:27,083
This could be our only chance
to get out of here.

213
00:11:28,209 --> 00:11:29,709
The way out is open.

214
00:11:31,167 --> 00:11:33,125
We have to move
while he's distracted.

215
00:11:33,459 --> 00:11:35,042
Spread the word. Quickly.

216
00:11:36,501 --> 00:11:39,291
It is your destiny
to struggle here.

217
00:11:39,292 --> 00:11:40,959
It is a form of my act.

218
00:11:41,250 --> 00:11:43,208
Hajrudin may bow to you,

219
00:11:43,209 --> 00:11:45,167
but I do not!

220
00:11:45,501 --> 00:11:46,626
[grunts]

221
00:11:51,792 --> 00:11:53,041
Hajrudin?

222
00:11:53,042 --> 00:11:56,209
If they know each other,
then who is this guy?

223
00:12:01,375 --> 00:12:05,209
Come on.
Show me your next move.

224
00:12:05,334 --> 00:12:07,042
[laughing mischievously]

225
00:12:07,709 --> 00:12:09,584
The wall is
right behind that big tree.

226
00:12:10,375 --> 00:12:12,709
Are you sure we can
get out of here fast enough?

227
00:12:12,834 --> 00:12:14,708
What do we do
if he catches us again?

228
00:12:14,709 --> 00:12:15,959
I won't let him!

229
00:12:17,375 --> 00:12:19,375
Watch! I'll hit it from here!

230
00:12:21,834 --> 00:12:23,834
Special Attack Green Star!

231
00:12:24,292 --> 00:12:27,167
Skull Bombgrass!

232
00:12:28,751 --> 00:12:31,751
[dramatic music]

233
00:12:59,834 --> 00:13:00,751
Huh?

234
00:13:03,542 --> 00:13:05,375
We sure made a mess, huh?

235
00:13:06,834 --> 00:13:09,333
Hey! We're sorry!

236
00:13:09,334 --> 00:13:10,875
Who the hell cares?

237
00:13:10,876 --> 00:13:11,875
I care!

238
00:13:11,876 --> 00:13:13,459
You blew up way too much stuff!

239
00:13:13,584 --> 00:13:16,249
I'm sorry I blew up
the Psycho's box set.

240
00:13:16,250 --> 00:13:17,667
As long as you're sorry.

241
00:13:17,918 --> 00:13:19,666
Anyway, look, Luffy.

242
00:13:19,667 --> 00:13:21,209
I broke the mirror part,

243
00:13:21,334 --> 00:13:23,459
but the wall looks
like it's rock-solid.

244
00:13:23,584 --> 00:13:25,000
Indeed, so.

245
00:13:25,334 --> 00:13:27,542
You can never hope to break it.

246
00:13:27,667 --> 00:13:30,292
None shall escape
from my garden.

247
00:13:30,459 --> 00:13:31,709
[laughing]

248
00:13:31,918 --> 00:13:34,209
Verily, they are too cool.

249
00:13:35,083 --> 00:13:37,584
Little Doll's defying
fate itself.

250
00:13:37,709 --> 00:13:39,625
Best episode ever!

251
00:13:39,626 --> 00:13:41,459
[cheering and applauding]

252
00:13:41,626 --> 00:13:43,584
[laughing]

253
00:13:44,042 --> 00:13:49,334
A proper world needs despair,
setbacks, disappointments.

254
00:13:49,626 --> 00:13:52,083
Good Lord is full of them.

255
00:13:52,209 --> 00:13:54,125
What the hell's
he going on about?

256
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:56,000
I've had enough of this guy.

257
00:13:57,417 --> 00:13:59,209
Cat, you okay?

258
00:13:59,459 --> 00:14:01,501
[meowing]

259
00:14:08,626 --> 00:14:10,166
Come on, Bouncer!

260
00:14:10,167 --> 00:14:11,208
He's so close!

261
00:14:11,209 --> 00:14:12,751
Wait while he's monologuing.

262
00:14:14,083 --> 00:14:16,249
He's going to catch up
at this rate.

263
00:14:16,250 --> 00:14:18,167
- What should we do?
- I'll stab him.

264
00:14:18,292 --> 00:14:19,709
- I'll kick him.
- Cat!

265
00:14:19,834 --> 00:14:21,250
[meowing]

266
00:14:21,375 --> 00:14:22,709
He says, "Shut up!"

267
00:14:23,125 --> 00:14:26,083
Weak and pathetic, yet so bold.

268
00:14:26,209 --> 00:14:30,000
It's me right in the fields,
my priceless collection.

269
00:14:30,125 --> 00:14:31,500
Ultra-rare Luffy!

270
00:14:31,501 --> 00:14:33,333
Ultra-rare Zoro!

271
00:14:33,334 --> 00:14:34,999
Ultra-rare Sanji!

272
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:36,626
Ultra-rare Usopp!

273
00:14:37,083 --> 00:14:38,834
Ultra-rare Chopper!

274
00:14:39,042 --> 00:14:40,250
Ultra-rare Nami!

275
00:14:40,375 --> 00:14:41,750
He knows who we are?

276
00:14:41,751 --> 00:14:43,959
There's something strange
going on here

277
00:14:44,209 --> 00:14:45,751
What's "ultra-rare"?

278
00:14:51,375 --> 00:14:54,167
[laughing]

279
00:14:55,792 --> 00:14:57,375
Did that idiot just trip?

280
00:14:57,626 --> 00:14:59,625
He'll still catch us
when he gets up.

281
00:14:59,626 --> 00:15:01,292
Somebody has to have a plan.

282
00:15:01,417 --> 00:15:02,834
Hey, Usopp.

283
00:15:03,042 --> 00:15:06,417
You can't blame someone
for a natural disaster, right?

284
00:15:06,542 --> 00:15:10,083
Uh, like earthquakes
and floods or a storm?

285
00:15:10,292 --> 00:15:12,875
Can't say that's
anyone's fault, but why?

286
00:15:12,876 --> 00:15:14,959
Nothing, it's just
that this guy seems

287
00:15:15,083 --> 00:15:17,459
bent on putting people
through hell.

288
00:15:22,209 --> 00:15:24,959
I'd go so far
as to say "He sucks"!

289
00:15:25,459 --> 00:15:28,291
He does,
but he's a giant, so we--

290
00:15:28,292 --> 00:15:29,501
I get it, Nami.

291
00:15:29,626 --> 00:15:30,709
I'm angry too.

292
00:15:31,125 --> 00:15:33,834
In fact, I've got a real grudge
against that creep

293
00:15:34,083 --> 00:15:35,999
because I realized something.

294
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:37,125
Something he did.

295
00:15:37,792 --> 00:15:40,667
He changed your clothes,
so I bet he saw you naked!

296
00:15:40,792 --> 00:15:41,876
Ugh.

297
00:15:43,918 --> 00:15:44,876
Let's kill him.

298
00:15:45,125 --> 00:15:46,833
No, Sanji, wait!

299
00:15:46,834 --> 00:15:48,500
We went over this! Listen to me!

300
00:15:48,501 --> 00:15:50,292
Tough luck,
I only listen to ladies!

301
00:15:50,417 --> 00:15:51,751
I'm with them, Sanji.

302
00:15:51,876 --> 00:15:52,750
Don't do it.

303
00:15:52,751 --> 00:15:53,626
Nami, why?

304
00:15:53,959 --> 00:15:55,501
Because you don't have to.

305
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:57,751
The heavens will make him pay.

306
00:15:57,918 --> 00:15:58,792
Huh?

307
00:15:59,292 --> 00:16:04,167
[heavy footsteps]

308
00:16:11,667 --> 00:16:14,083
[squawking]

309
00:16:23,792 --> 00:16:26,626
Boogie, have you
brought me another gift?

310
00:16:26,751 --> 00:16:28,417
It's no small prize.

311
00:16:28,584 --> 00:16:29,876
What could it be?

312
00:16:35,375 --> 00:16:39,209
[ALL snoring]

313
00:16:39,584 --> 00:16:42,374
Whoa, these are
the Straw Hat Pirates!

314
00:16:42,375 --> 00:16:44,625
But aren't they supposed
to be under the care

315
00:16:44,626 --> 00:16:46,374
of the giant pirate crew
right now?

316
00:16:46,375 --> 00:16:48,417
How the heck did you
end up with them?

317
00:16:50,375 --> 00:16:51,959
Does anyone know
they're missing?

318
00:16:52,250 --> 00:16:53,834
They're sleeping pretty soundly.

319
00:16:54,083 --> 00:16:56,625
Did they perchance pass through
the Sleeping Mists

320
00:16:56,626 --> 00:16:57,876
on their way from Egghead?

321
00:16:59,584 --> 00:17:01,959
[laughing]

322
00:17:02,250 --> 00:17:04,667
What an unexpected turn
of fortune!

323
00:17:05,083 --> 00:17:07,042
The Straw Hats, hmm?

324
00:17:08,709 --> 00:17:09,918
To be frank, when I heard

325
00:17:10,042 --> 00:17:12,417
that Hajrudin had become
Straw Hat's underling

326
00:17:12,542 --> 00:17:13,918
without a word to us,

327
00:17:14,083 --> 00:17:16,375
I found it quite irksome.

328
00:17:18,459 --> 00:17:20,125
Hey, wait, Hajrudin!

329
00:17:20,292 --> 00:17:21,500
I heard the news.

330
00:17:21,501 --> 00:17:22,876
Are you out of your mind?

331
00:17:23,542 --> 00:17:26,333
I'm a member of
the New Giant Warrior Pirates,

332
00:17:26,334 --> 00:17:27,959
so I'd end up as underling too.

333
00:17:28,167 --> 00:17:32,042
Why should we warriors of Elbaph
have to serve a puny human?

334
00:17:32,751 --> 00:17:35,959
These idiots have no pride!

335
00:17:37,459 --> 00:17:40,667
Look at you, so tiny
and weak and pathetic.

336
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:44,584
Fast asleep as the jaws of death
close in on you.

337
00:17:45,083 --> 00:17:46,584
Oh-oh!

338
00:17:47,250 --> 00:17:49,042
[laughing]

339
00:17:49,584 --> 00:17:50,959
But you,

340
00:17:51,167 --> 00:17:53,334
you are my new fave!

341
00:17:53,501 --> 00:17:55,667
Ultra-rare Nami!

342
00:17:55,792 --> 00:17:57,292
Ooh!

343
00:17:57,667 --> 00:17:58,667
Oops!

344
00:17:58,876 --> 00:18:02,292
[humming]

345
00:18:04,626 --> 00:18:06,292
[laughing]

346
00:18:10,751 --> 00:18:12,834
I'll let you sleep a bit longer.

347
00:18:12,959 --> 00:18:15,834
You'll have a big surprise
when you wake up.

348
00:18:16,417 --> 00:18:17,709
[laughing]

349
00:18:17,876 --> 00:18:19,125
If you stay missing,

350
00:18:19,250 --> 00:18:21,626
no one will be able
to raise her.

351
00:18:22,417 --> 00:18:24,083
I won't be your underling,

352
00:18:24,209 --> 00:18:26,250
but I'm happy
to be your overlord!

353
00:18:26,375 --> 00:18:29,042
All the fun will happen
in my playground!

354
00:18:29,167 --> 00:18:30,083
[gasps]

355
00:18:35,709 --> 00:18:38,542
What? I don't remember
making these clouds.

356
00:18:39,167 --> 00:18:41,626
You ready to rain
on his parade, Zeus?

357
00:18:43,918 --> 00:18:46,459
Yep, I'm fully charged.

358
00:18:47,417 --> 00:18:49,000
Then he is all yours.

359
00:18:50,792 --> 00:18:52,584
Lightning Blast!

360
00:18:54,209 --> 00:18:57,918
Here we go!

361
00:18:58,834 --> 00:19:02,334
[screaming]

362
00:19:26,459 --> 00:19:28,167
[meowing]

363
00:19:36,667 --> 00:19:37,959
Nami!

364
00:19:38,083 --> 00:19:39,542
That's too much!

365
00:19:39,667 --> 00:19:41,709
Are you crazy?

366
00:19:44,209 --> 00:19:45,374
Why, Usopp?

367
00:19:45,375 --> 00:19:47,291
I don't know
what you're talking about.

368
00:19:47,292 --> 00:19:48,500
People act up

369
00:19:48,501 --> 00:19:50,459
and the heavens
strike them down.

370
00:19:50,626 --> 00:19:52,041
You struck him down!

371
00:19:52,042 --> 00:19:53,042
You get that!

372
00:19:54,918 --> 00:19:58,501
All right, keep running
all the way to that wall!

373
00:19:58,834 --> 00:20:01,000
[meowing]

374
00:20:07,542 --> 00:20:08,959
Jump, Cat, jump!

375
00:20:10,417 --> 00:20:13,417
[meowing]

376
00:20:17,834 --> 00:20:21,667
[laughing] Mini Fourth Gear!

377
00:20:26,959 --> 00:20:29,374
This Block Kingdom
has been pretty fun,

378
00:20:29,375 --> 00:20:30,959
but we're out of here!

379
00:20:31,459 --> 00:20:33,000
It's about damn time.

380
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:35,834
So long, giant perv.

381
00:20:36,125 --> 00:20:39,292
Please let it be Elbaph
out there, please!

382
00:20:42,375 --> 00:20:45,167
Gum-Gum...

383
00:20:45,667 --> 00:20:49,000
Kong Gun!

384
00:21:04,250 --> 00:21:07,250
[cheering]

385
00:21:23,375 --> 00:21:26,709
<i>Here I am straining
Both my eyes</i>

386
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:32,375
<i>And checking
Where I am standing right now</i>

387
00:21:34,334 --> 00:21:38,584
<i>With my brain consumed
By all the delusion and despair</i>

388
00:21:38,792 --> 00:21:42,042
<i>I'm always bound
To be a little off somehow</i>

389
00:21:42,501 --> 00:21:46,000
<i>The things that come up vividly</i>

390
00:21:47,918 --> 00:21:51,375
<i>Are always the cruel memories</i>

391
00:21:53,459 --> 00:21:55,333
<i>I gather up the scraps</i>

392
00:21:55,334 --> 00:21:57,501
<i>Of the simple boredom
Of my life</i>

393
00:21:57,751 --> 00:22:01,584
<i>I might turn
Into somebody else but me</i>

394
00:22:02,834 --> 00:22:05,751
<i>I wonder which future
Would fit someone like me now</i>

395
00:22:05,918 --> 00:22:08,918
<i>From here on no matter how hard
I try to strain my eyes</i>

396
00:22:09,042 --> 00:22:12,125
<i>I'll still see nothing anyhow</i>

397
00:22:12,250 --> 00:22:15,584
<i>I'm riding the headwind</i>

398
00:22:15,876 --> 00:22:18,501
<i>I pour it into the tear
Of destiny</i>

399
00:22:18,667 --> 00:22:23,000
<i>As I split
All the false fantasies apart</i>

400
00:22:23,125 --> 00:22:26,626
<i>And everyone's</i>

401
00:22:26,751 --> 00:22:29,416
<i>Piling up
Their own life-or-death reality</i>

402
00:22:29,417 --> 00:22:31,375
<i>All the time just like that</i>

403
00:22:31,501 --> 00:22:33,792
<i>Then tomorrow comes
Way too loud</i>

404
00:22:33,918 --> 00:22:38,083
<i>Leaving no time
Even just to pray</i>

405
00:22:38,334 --> 00:22:42,667
<i>And that future we see</i>

406
00:22:43,042 --> 00:22:46,501
<i>It all belongs to me</i>

407
00:22:54,834 --> 00:22:56,791
<i>Bursting out
of the Block Kingdom,</i>

408
00:22:56,792 --> 00:22:59,417
<i>the Straw Hats are met
with an endless snowy expanse.</i>

409
00:22:59,542 --> 00:23:01,917
<i>Uncertain if they are welcome
in this land,</i>

410
00:23:01,918 --> 00:23:03,208
<i>they proceed with caution</i>

411
00:23:03,209 --> 00:23:05,541
<i>until Luffy hears
the same ominous roar</i>

412
00:23:05,542 --> 00:23:07,333
<i>that rang out
in the Block Kingdom.</i>

413
00:23:07,334 --> 00:23:10,626
<i>Venturing forth on his own,
he seeks to find its source.</i>

414
00:23:10,751 --> 00:23:12,334
On the next One Piece!

415
00:23:12,459 --> 00:23:14,374
An Encounter on A Snowfield

416
00:23:14,375 --> 00:23:16,626
Loki, The Accursed Prince.

417
00:23:16,876 --> 00:23:19,292
I'm going to be
King of the Pirates!

